    <string name="tutorial_budget_title">What is a budget?</string>
    <string name="tutorial_budget_description">A budget is a plan for your money. Your monthly spending limit is the amount you choose to make available for spending—it stays separate from income unless you explicitly include an income transaction.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_monthly_budget_title">Set your monthly budget</string>
    <string name="tutorial_home_title">Read your Home screen</string>
    <string name="tutorial_home_coach">%1$s shows the month at a glance: income in, expenses out, and the spending limit kept separate. Try Good, Neutral, and Bad above.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_try_three_states">Try each example in the real screen</string>
    <string name="tutorial_state_good">Good</string>
    <string name="tutorial_state_neutral">Neutral</string>
    <string name="tutorial_state_bad">Bad</string>
    <string name="tutorial_demo_analytics_header_state">%1$.2f%% of %2$s1,000.00 used</string>
    <string name="tutorial_monthly_budget_description">Open Monthly Budget from the wallet icon. Choose the month, enter a spending limit, optionally divide it among categories, then save. A spending limit works even with no category allocations.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_transaction_title">Add a transaction</string>
    <string name="tutorial_transaction_description">Tap the plus button, choose Expense or Income, enter the amount and date, and select a category. You can also attach a receipt image. Income is added to the spending limit only when you turn that option on.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_ocr_title">Scan receipts offline</string>
    <string name="tutorial_ocr_description">Use the camera icon on Home for a quick scan, or choose Scan receipt with OCR while adding a transaction. The recognised merchant, date, total, and category fill the transaction automatically. You can turn confirmation back on in Settings. A missing date uses today, an unmatched category uses your OCR default, and every scan keeps its OCR tag for filtering.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_analytics_title">Read your analytics</string>
    <string name="tutorial_analytics_description">The gauge shows how much of the effective spending limit has been used. Charts break expenses down by category, while income, expenses, remaining allowance, and net cash flow stay clearly separated.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_records_title">Filter and view records</string>
    <string name="tutorial_records_description">Tap Records on Home to open history. Filter by All, Income, Expense, OCR, or a date range. Tap a Home record to view only that record; in history, tap to edit or press and hold to delete.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_budget_welcome">Hi %2$s! I’m %1$s. A budget is simply your plan for your money. Choose how much you are comfortable spending this month, then use categories only if they help you. Your income stays separate unless you decide to add it to the limit.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_budget_coach">Set a monthly spending limit, then optionally divide it among categories. The real budget controls remain visible while %1$s guides you.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_transaction_coach">Choose Expense or Income, enter an amount, then select a date and category. These are the same controls used for a real transaction.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_ocr_coach">Take a photo or choose one from Gallery. %1$s reads it offline and fills the transaction form for you.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_analytics_coach">The needle shows the exact percentage used. Gauge colours come from Settings; try the three examples above.</string>
    <string name="tutorial_records_coach">Records contain every saved transaction. Filter All, Income, Expenses, OCR, or a date range, then open any record for details.</string>
